Overview
This PR fixes critical issues preventing the non-custodial 0G chat system from working correctly. The main problems were ESM import errors causing "exports is not defined" browser crashes, improper prepared request validation, SSR hydration issues with the LedgerBalance component, and excessive ENOENT error spam in server logs.

Issues Fixed
1. ESM Import Error ("exports is not defined")
Problem: Browser crashes with exports is not defined when attempting to use 0G SDK

// Before: Static import causing SSR issues
import { createZGComputeNetworkBroker } from '@0glabs/0g-serving-broker'
Solution: Implemented proper dynamic client-side imports with SSR guards

// After: Dynamic import with client-side guard
if (typeof window !== 'undefined') {
  const brokerModule = await import('@0glabs/0g-serving-broker')
  const { createZGComputeNetworkBroker } = brokerModule
}
Updated next.config.js to properly transpile SDK packages:

transpilePackages: ["@0glabs/0g-serving-broker", "@0glabs/0g-serving-user-broker"]
2. Non-Custodial Request Validation
Problem: API wasn't properly validating prepared requests for non-custodial mode

// Before: Inconsistent validation logic
if (useNonCustodial) {
  // Missing proper prepared request check
}
Solution: Added proper validation with correct logging chain

// After: Proper validation and logging
if (useNonCustodial && !prep) {
  console.log('[CHAT] HIT - non-custodial mode required but no prepared request provided')
  return NextResponse.json({
    error: 'non_custodial_required',
    requiresPreparedRequest: true
  }, { status: 400 })
}
3. LedgerBalance Component SSR Issues
Problem: Component trying to access wallet during SSR causing hydration mismatches

// Before: Immediate wallet access
useEffect(() => {
  if (isConnected && address) {
    loadLedgerInfo() // Runs during SSR
  }
}, [isConnected, address])
Solution: Added proper client-side rendering guards

// After: Client-side guard with auto-ledger creation
const [isClient, setIsClient] = useState(false)

useEffect(() => {
  setIsClient(true) // Ensure client-side only
}, [])

useEffect(() => {
  if (isClient && isConnected && address) {
    loadLedgerInfo() // Only runs on client
  }
}, [isClient, isConnected, address])
4. ENOENT Error Spam Cleanup
Problem: Server logs flooded with ENOENT errors for missing metadata files

// Before: Noisy error logging
} catch (fileError: any) {
  console.log('[Storage Retrieve] Local file not found:', cleanRootHash)
  if (fileError.code === 'ENOENT') {
    console.log('[Storage Retrieve] ENOENT - File does not exist, will use fallback')
  }
}
Solution: Silent fallback for expected missing files

// After: Quiet fallback logging
} catch (fileError: any) {
  if (fileError.code === 'ENOENT') {
    console.log('[Storage Retrieve] Local file not found, falling back to indexer')
  } else {
    console.log('[Storage Retrieve] File access error:', fileError.message)
  }
}
